think Standfast: verified the living REDS rows. Row 85's place_paint red is Closed and conic_paint/compose_tiled are already converted to native contains; the remaining fragile printf-'%s'-single-quote-grep pattern lives only in ~24 HUNK witnesses which are currently GREEN -- a ratchet (convert on touch, books nothing), not an open red. So Standfast is genuinely clear and I took the next constructive lap rather than proactively sweeping untouched witnesses (the ratchet turns on touch, not by a sweep).
think Chose the crux: line_slice, the pencil read. The single-line-over-scene family is complete and line_cross lifted to two lines; the natural fold on top reads ONE stroke as an ordered CUT -- the objects the FINITE stroke pierces, in stroke order. Decisive because it is a FILTER of the order, not a new geometry: line_pierce.pierced_labels re-sorted by line_order.project_label with the SAME (projection, label) tie-break, so line_slice is provably the SUBSEQUENCE of line_order restricted to the pierced set. No new math, exact integers, compose-not-braid over two green-witnessed neighbors.
think Confirmed both neighbors index the same object-label space (1..components): line_pierce.pierce_flags/pierced_labels walk per label, line_order.project_label/line_order rank per label. So the filter composes cleanly. Confirmed pierces is the FINITE predicate (seg-bbox-overlap AND straddle) and line_pierces the infinite (straddle only), so is_sliced = pierces.
think Designed a decisive selftest scene (30x14, six 2x2 singletons): four on row 10 sliced by the horizontal A->B, U high off the line, Z on row 10 beyond the B end. Full order [A,P,U,Q,B,Z], finite slice [A,P,Q,B]; U leaves for being OFF the line (line_pierces FALSE), Z for being PAST the finite end (line_pierces TRUE, pierce_only_infinite TRUE) -- two different exclusion reasons, both present in line_order and absent from line_slice. Labels derived from taps via hit_test.object_label_at, no fragile raster assumption.
obs Surface: line_slice (the ordered cut), slice_count, is_sliced, slice_rank (NotPierced when missed), first_sliced/last_sliced (SliceEmpty when empty), slice_reads_before. Refusals SameGroup/EmptyClick/PointOutOfBounds/BadTarget inherited through the composed calls. GREEN on the FIRST full metal run of both selftest and witness, no code reds.
